# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SilverCare — Environment Variable Guide (NO SECRETS in this file)
# Copy this file to `.env` locally, then fill in YOUR real values.
# On Railway: Service → Variables → add each variable listed below.
# NEVER commit `.env` or `serviceAccountKey.json` (both are git-ignored).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ── How to find each value ───────────────────────────────────────
#  • SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON — Firebase Console → Project settings →
#    Service accounts → Generate new private key → paste ENTIRE JSON
#    on ONE line (keep \n inside private_key as literal \n).
#  • FIREBASE_* — Firebase Console → Project settings → General →
#    Your web app config (public values, also in public/js/firebase-config.js).
#  • FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL — Realtime Database URL, e.g.
#    https://silvercare-a89e6-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app
#    (Firebase Console → Build → Realtime Database → URL shown at the top).
#    For this project it MUST be the asia-southeast1 URL — the
#    default-region fallback (…-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com) is wrong.
#  • EMAIL_USER / EMAIL_PASS — Gmail address + Gmail APP password
#    (Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App passwords).
#  • TEXTBEE_API_KEY / TEXTBEE_DEVICE_ID — TextBee Dashboard
#    (https://textbee.dev) → your paired Android phone → the API key and
#    device ID shown there. The Android phone sends the texts, so it must
#    stay on with a working SIM. See the SMS section further down.
#  • SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — Supabase Dashboard →
#    Project Settings → API → Project URL + service_role key (NOT anon).
#    Then run scripts/supabase-setup.sql once in the Supabase SQL Editor.
#  • QR_SECRET — any long random string. Generate one with:
#      node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#  • PUBLIC_BASE_URL — your Railway public URL, no trailing slash, e.g.
#      https://silver-production-xxxx.up.railway.app

# ── Deployment identity (REQUIRED for production links/CORS) ──
# Your Railway public URL, e.g. https://silvercare-production.up.railway.app
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# ── Deployment mode ──
# Set to "production" on Railway. This activates production CORS behavior
# (dev-only localhost origins are disabled) — safe even if you forget.
# NODE_ENV=production

# ── Firebase Admin (server) ────────────────────────────────────
# Paste the ENTIRE serviceAccountKey.json content on ONE line.
SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# NOTE: for this project FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL (in the web-config section
# below) is REQUIRED anyway — the database lives in asia-southeast1, so the
# default-region fallback URL built from the project ID alone would point
# at the wrong region. Set it there, not here.

# ── Firebase Web config (served at /js/firebase-config.js) ────
FIREBASE_API_KEY=
FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
FIREBASE_APP_ID=
FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# REQUIRED for this project — must be the asia-southeast1 URL:
# https://silvercare-a89e6-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app
FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=

# ── E-mail delivery ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Railway BLOCKS outbound SMTP (ports 25/465/587) on Free/Trial/Hobby
# plans — Gmail SMTP will ALWAYS time out there, no matter how correct
# EMAIL_USER/EMAIL_PASS are. You MUST use an HTTPS e-mail API instead.
# Recommended: Brevo (free, 300 e-mails/day, your Gmail as sender):
#   1. Sign up at https://www.brevo.com/ (free, no credit card)
#   2. Verify your sender: Login > Settings (gear) > Senders & IP >
#      Add a sender = your Gmail address > click the confirmation link
#      Brevo e-mails to that Gmail inbox
#   3. Get the key: SMTP & API > API Keys > Generate a new API key
#   4. On Railway add:  BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-...  (paste the key)
# Alternative: Resend (free 100/day, needs domain verification for
# custom senders — Brevo is easier for a Gmail sender):
#   1. Sign up at https://resend.com/ > API Keys > Create API Key
#   2. On Railway add:  RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# NOTE: if BOTH keys are set, Brevo wins. If NEITHER is set, the app
# falls back to Gmail SMTP (works locally and on Railway Pro only).
BREVO_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to EMAIL_USER if unset. Must be a Brevo-verified sender.
# BREVO_SENDER=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to onboarding@resend.dev (test only).
# RESEND_FROM=

# ── Gmail SMTP (local dev / Railway Pro fallback) ─────────────
# Only used when NEITHER Brevo nor Resend key is set.
EMAIL_USER=
EMAIL_PASS=

# ── SMS delivery (TextBee — seniors are texted on their CP number) ──
# Every senior gets a text when their account is verified, when their
# pension is approved / releasing / released (or declined), and for
# assistance claims. The number is ALWAYS read from the senior's own
# profile (users/{uid}/cpNumber) — no route can text an arbitrary number.
#
# Why TextBee: Railway also blocks outbound SMS gateways, but TextBee is a
# plain HTTPS API (port 443), so it works on every Railway plan. TextBee
# queues each message to an Android phone you pair; that phone sends it
# through its own SIM — no per-message fee, only your normal load.
#   1. Install the TextBee app on an Android phone with an active SIM
#      (https://textbee.dev — app available on Google Play / APK).
#   2. Sign up at https://textbee.dev, then pair the phone (scan the QR).
#   3. Copy the API key from the dashboard (starts with "tb_") and the
#      device ID of the paired phone.
#   4. On Railway add:  TEXTBEE_API_KEY=...  and  TEXTBEE_DEVICE_ID=...
# Leave TEXTBEE_API_KEY blank to disable SMS entirely — the app still runs
# and every status change continues to work, it simply skips the text.
# Check which mode you are in any time at /api/sms-status (no secrets).
TEXTBEE_API_KEY=
# Optional — pin the sending phone when several are paired. Only needed
# when more than one device is registered on the account.
# TEXTBEE_DEVICE_ID=
# Optional — only for a self-hosted TextBee instance. Defaults to
# https://api.textbee.dev/api/v1 and never needs to be set for textbee.dev.
# TEXTBEE_BASE_URL=

# ── Supabase (senior data mirror + ID/medical vaults) ──────────
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── QR verification ────────────────────────────────────────────
QR_SECRET=

# ── Optional: extra allowed origins (comma-separated) ──────────
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-custom-domain.com
